laws "Rust Service Laws" version 1

law private-work-is-private
  says "An admin never reads another user's Private Work."
  why  "Private Work is personal, even inside an organisation account."
  on   action read of PrivateWork
  forbid when resource.owner != principal
  permit when resource.owner == principal
  evidence proved by kani "auth::private_work_read_holds" in "crates/core"

law auth-invariants-proved
  says "Authorization decisions fail closed on missing or invalid claims."
  why  "Security boundaries must be mathematically verified, not guessed."
  on   code "src/auth/**"
  evidence proved by kani "auth::fail_closed_verdict" in "."

law unit-suite-guards-core
  says "Core domain logic passes the full Rust test suite before merge."
  why  "Prevent regressions across state transitions and parsers."
  on   code "src/**"
  evidence tested by command "cargo test --locked"
